    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div bgcolor=\"white\" lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Hi Stefanie,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">I’m not familiar with the newick format but the tree in Canopy is coded as a list embedded with tree elements and is plotted using R package ape. I am not sure\r\n why you want to use bootstrap on the tree, but if you want to get the confidence intervals or standard errors, since we are using the MCMC sampling procedure, you can get these by looking at the posterior distribution after binning and thinning. If you still\r\n want bootstrap, you will most likely have to code yourself from the tree, which again, is a list object in R.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Hope that this clarifies! I am cc’ing our mailing list in case other users have similar questions.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Best,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Yuchao<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #e1e1e1 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0in 0in 0in\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:windowtext\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:windowtext\"> Stefanie Friedrich [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">stefanie....@dbb.su.se</a>]\r\n<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Wednesday, March 15, 2017 2:56 PM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> Jiang, Yuchao &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">yuc...@wharton.upenn.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> Canopy - bootstrapping<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p>Dear Yuchao Jiang,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p>My name is Stefanie Friedrich and I am working with mutations and cancer heterogeneity.\r\n<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p>I would like to have bootstrap values for the output tree. Is it possible to apply bootstrapping on the output tree?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p>Another possibility would be to print the tree in an appropriate format and to calculate bootstrap values on my own. Is it possible to print the tree in newick format for example?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p>Kind regards<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p>Stefanie<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">-- <br>\r\n<br>\r\n<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p>M. Sc., Ph.D. student <br>\r\nStockholm bioinformatics center, <a href=\"http://sonnhammer.sbc.su.se/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://sonnhammer.sbc.su.se/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792498492474000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Rtabvu4H7T1pPdUYgnpui\"><i>Sonnhammer group\r\n</i></a><br>\r\nDepartment of Biochemistry and Biophysics, Stockholm University <br>\r\n<br>\r\nScience for Life Laboratory | Tomtebodavägen 23 | SE-171 65 Solna <br>\r\n<br>\r\ne-mail: <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\"><span style=\"text-decoration:none\">Stefanie....@dbb.su.se</span></a>\r\n<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n"
    ]
